{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"8887fbbe5f65528d132759ba2cee85e246e5f487d882fd2d894f2282329cb59d","digest":{"component_or_area":"rebar search / identifier resolution","key_entities":["reducer/search.py::_haystack","_engine_support/reads.py::search_state","_ids.py::_resolve_via_binding_store","_ids.py::binding_jira_key_map","ticket_id","alias","jira_key","state.get","_query.parse_query","binding_reverse map","tests/unit/test_search_identifiers.py","tests/interfaces/queries/test_ws5a_search.py"],"problem_keywords":["search","identifier matching","ticket id","alias","jira key","haystack","case-insensitivity"],"propositions":["rebar search does not match tickets by their canonical ticket_id, human alias, or bound Jira key because _haystack excludes these identifiers from the searchable text","when a user runs rebar search with a Jira key (e.g. REB-1654), it returns empty results even though rebar show REB-1654 correctly resolves the ticket","the Jira key binding lives only in the binding store, not in the reduced state, so search_states cannot access it without breaking purity","identifier matching must be case-insensitive so 'search REB-1654' and 'search reb-1654' both surface the same ticket, mirroring show behavior","the fix enriches states with jira_key in the caller search_state before passing to the pure search_states function, avoiding filesystem access inside the reducer"]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787652529362884001,"uuid":"90e30dd6-379e-4fc8-9403-e1d13975130b"}